# UBSan suppressions for the port's sanitizer run (tests/port/run.py --sanitize; psxstack's port_test passes the file
# as UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...). psxstack's docs/PORT.md "Compiling the game C for the host": only out-of-bounds
# indexes of the game's own C that stay inside one struct whose layout is the same on the host, so the host computes
# what the PS1 computes. Each line names the function and the finding (docs/PORT.md "Testing").
#
# assignCardCopySerial (src/main/card/card_db.c), from resetPlayerData's j < 8: each card gets 8 serials in a
# u16 cardCopySerials[301][6] row, so copies 6 and 7 land on the next card's copies 0 and 1 (which that card's own
# turn rewrites) and the last card's on areaScriptFlags[0] (which resetScriptProgress zeroes after). Both inside
# PlayerProfile, whose bytes from bonusCounts to unk2435 have the PS1's layout on the host (port/game/state.c).
bounds:assignCardCopySerial
